Introduction
Social media is something that connects us all, something most of us can't live without.
It is a tool in our society that is relatively new however it is growing rapidly.
To start what is social media? Why is it something that is so important to us in our society?

Social media would be defined as a space where users are able interact and self present in whatever way they would like, 
from present time or asynchronously through channels on the internet ,
presenting to either large or narrow groups of individuals/audiences who find importance or interest from the content generated 
and a level of perceived interaction with others through the internet. (Carr and Hayes, 2015) 

Examples such as FaceBook, MySpace, Whatsapp, Snapchat and many more are social media platforms which mainly rely
on methods in which individuals can communicate with each other. From texts to call/video calls, voice messages. These social media 
platforms can also focus on how an individual can communicate with a wider audience in methods like Photo or video posts on Facebook and Instagram, Stories
like on Snapchat, Whatsapp status and Instagram stories. 

This is something that has changed the way humans communicate with each other both in business and societal ways.
In this case study we will be exploring the societal and business viewpoint in relation to the 'Evolution of social media' and their impacts and
we will also be discussing the ethical reflections and the improvements in social media as of recently.

First viewpoint analysis:
With the evolution of social media came with impacts on how companies run their businesses and how society functions around the usage of social media.
For businesses, social media brought new ways to advertise and sell products for customers to buy. On the societal aspect, it was able to allow
people new ways to communicate with each other, as well as making it easier to talk to other people from around the globe. 

A way that major brands were able to bring more attention to their business was through advertisements on social media platforms. Advertisements on social
media was introduced as early as 2006 with Facebook, after that was Twitter enabling ads in 2010, then other sites such as Snapchat, Youtube and more adding
ads to their platforms. Companies saw this as an opportunity to make their brands more popular, so they started to use social media as a way to grow. So they started
putting ads on these sites either in picture or video form to inform people about their products, or recruit them for their company. Even making the some of the ads
entaining to some degree to entice people. Other social media sites even created accounts on their competitors websites to advertise and talk about upcoming updates
to their own platforms.

Ethical Reflection & Improvements
Social media has developed significantly from MySpace to Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok. These platfroms have made communication easier and allow people to share information, photos and videos worldwide. 
